Chapter 13
When we arrive in the present we are welcomed by the gang members.
Ray: Woah! What happened?! Y'all look totally battered!
Seth: Boss! Hurry Lu, get her a blood pack!
While Lu hastily gets the blood pack the other two help me get Scarlet to the sofa and we sit her down gently.
Ray: Looks like ya still had to fight that bastard. Your wounds are at the same place as your scars from before.
Seth: But they look more fresh and deep right now. It's a miracle that you're still alive. He had a silver sword, right?
(t): Do I tell them that I let her suck my blood?…
(t): I don't know if that gesture is seen as something intimate or if it's normal. I don't want to make her feel awkward…
I take a few seconds before I finally decide.
CHOICE OPTION 1: I'll just tell the truth.
(t): They're bound to find out one way or another.
Me: I had Scarlet drink my blood because she was on the brink of death.
I sigh and turn my head so they can see the bite mark.
Everyone makes a surprised face, except for Scarlet.
She's distracted with opening the blood pack and sticking a straw in.
Ray: WHA— Boss??? She drank it? From you?
(t): What's that reaction? I better not tell him anything more about that. Seems like my hunch from before was actually right.
I feel my face getting hot again.
(t): I can't help it, now I'm thinking about that moment again.
Seth: Right, this comes as a surprise.
Ray: Wait, hold up. Why are you blushin' so hard? Somethin happen between you two? Besides the blood sucking?
He looks back and forth between me and Scarlet with a smug expression on his face.
ILLUSTRATION
Me: Um, no?
I try to avoid everyone's intense gazes.
Now Scarlet turns her face to us.
She seems to have noticed what our conversation is about because her cheeks are red as well.
Scarlet: What are you guys so worked up about? I had no other choice but to drink {playerName}'s blood. We were both in no condition to shift. Though, I did get a little lost in the sensation…
She awkwardly looks away.
(t): Aww. How cute.
I chuckle at her visible shyness and watch her gulp down the blood from the pack.
CHOICE OPTION 2: I'll let Scarlet handle this.
(t): She knows better about stuff concerning vampire behaviour after all.
I stay quiet and watch Scarlet drink her blood pack in peace.
I feel relieved now that we're safe.
Then Lu points at me.
Lu: You're bleeding. Are you okay? Need me to get you a band aid?
I cover the bite wound on my neck with my hand.
(t): Oh. Now they'll find out.
I glance over at Scarlet and she meets my gaze.
Ray: What? What is it?
Scarlet lets out a sigh and throws the empty blood packet in the bin.
Scarlet: I had to drink {playerName}'s blood. Seth can you bring me the first aid kit? I'll take care of it.
They all stare at Scarlet with a shocked expression.
Ray: You? Drank blood? Not out of a pack, but like, straight out of {playerName}?
Scarlet: Couldn't be helped. I was in bad shape.
Seth: That's… surprising.
CONTINUE HERE AFTER CHOICE OPTIONS
Lu: I'm impressed. Until now, nobody from the gang could make her drink from a live body.
Me: Huh? Why?
(t): Is that why they're so surprised? True, Scarlet did say that it's been a long time since she drank blood straight from the vein.
Scarlet: These guys don't remember because they are young, but I remember a time where we were hunted because humans were scared of us. They saw us as monsters. I promised myself to never hurt somebody just to get blood. That's why the organisation has connections with hospitals so we can get the blood without causing anyone any harm.
It doesn't really surprise me.
(t): This confirms that Scarlet is a gentle and lovable soul. That's why I like her so much.
Seth comes back with the first aid kit.
Seth: The boss usually even avoids drinking the blood of animals directly from the body. Some vampires like the feeling of sinking their teeth into the prey. You could say it's instinctual. But Scarlet only relies on the packs, even in dire situations.
Ray: Well, looks like this time was different, right bo—
Before anyone has the chance of uttering any more words, a familiar dark mist appears and several cloaked figures emerge from it.
(t): The Interdimensional Spirits!
I try to think of what to do but they spread out faster than I can react.
It doesn't even take a single second for them to surround us and take hold of each of us.
Me: Scarlet!
The cloaked figure behind Scarlet points a sharp object that looks like a black dagger made out of fog to her head.
Scarlet remains calm.
(t): She must still be exhausted from the fight with Amon.
I see Ray, Seth and Lu struggle but they can't break free.
???: Sustainer. We've come to negotiate.
One of the figures approaches me.
Me: Let them go. I know you're not after them.
???: That is correct. But we've come to know that the woman over there is quite important to you. We will give you two choices.
The room becomes dead silent.
???: Your first option is to quietly come with us. Nothing bad will happen, they will all stay alive. Only you will be captured.
Scarlet looks at me and shakes her head.
Me: What if I won't go with you?
???: My friend over there will kill them on the spot. The first one to go will be the woman.
I look at Scarlet and the dagger is almost touching her temple.
Me: I won't let you hurt her. Not her and not anyone else.
???: Then you simply have to come with us.
Scarlet: No! You don't know what these monsters will do to you once they take you away!
(t): She's right, but I can't just let her and the guys die. They could kill them in an instant and I won't be fast enough to stop them.
Me: It's fine, Scarlet. I will find a way.
???: Is that your choice? If it is, then step inside.
A portal appears in front of my feet on the ground.
(t): I can only see darkness in there.
Scarlet: No! If they are willing to make a deal, they have a way to keep you there. They might even kill you! I won't let that happen.
???: What do you think you can do about it? You don't have the strength to fight us right now. Neither does the Sustainer.
(t): The figure didn't deny anything Scarlet just said. Then I'd prefer it if I died instead of Scarlet.
Scarlet: Just kill me right now! I don't care. {playerName}, you will find a way as long as they stay here and the others in the gang will avenge me.
Fear flickers in the faces of the three guys who have been quietly watching, also with a dagger pointed to their heads.
???: You foolish little thing. Those three will be dead just a few seconds after you. But of course, we would prefer the less violent choice.
The entity turns back to me.
(t): I won't let her sacrifice herself. I don't know what will happen if I enter the portal but at least that will prevent her immediate death. And if she dies, I wouldn't know how to live on…
Me: I'm sorry, Scarlet. I'll try to be back as fast as I can.
Scarlet: No! You did enough for me. Why do you always put me first? This could really be the end for you.
Me: It's because I love you!
(t): I actually said it.
The room is silent again.
(t): Well, if I die, at least I was able to get that off my chest.
Scarlet's eyes are wide open and she stares at me in shock.
???: Sustainer, we don't have all day.
(t): Ugh, way to kill the mood.
I look at Scarlet one last time and etch her features into my memory, in case this really is the last time I'll see her.
I smile at her reassuringly.
Me: Take care of yourself Scarlet.
With that, I step into the portal and let myself fall.
The cloaked figures all follow.
(t): Good. Looks like they really left them alone now.
Before the darkness completely engulfs me, I hear Scarlet yell out my name in despair.
(t): I'll just have to fight to death if that's what it takes to get back to you.
A faint whisper escapes my lips.
Me: I will always find my way back to you. Even when I'm dead.
